### Verdict: CHERRY_PICKING

### Justification
The claim's assertion that French visa cancellations and deportations of Pakistani citizens were **"due to" Imran Khan's criticism of Macron** is entirely unsupported by evidence. While Macron did make controversial comments about Islam in October 2020 ([India Today](https://www.indiatoday.in/world/story/backlash-over-french-president-emmanuel-macron-comment-on-islam-explained-boycottfrenchproducts-1735400-2020-10-27)) and Khan did publicly criticize those remarks ([MM News](https://mmnews.tv/pm-imran-lashes-out-at-french-president-macron-for-anti-muslim-attitude/)), and the Pakistani Consulate in France did publish a tweet on October 31, 2020 about visa cancellations ([archived tweet](https://web.archive.org/web/20210629013122/https://twitter.com/PakConsulateFr/status/1322495811993903104)), the French government never issued any official statement confirming, explaining, or justifying these actions. The Consulate itself acknowledged that "no clarification has yet [been] provided by the French immigration department regarding the visa cancellation of our citizens," and no source establishes a causal link between Khan's criticism and the French immigration actions. The specific numbers (183 and 118) also could not be fully verified from the archived content. Attributing the visa cancellations to Khan's criticism presents a partial situation in a way that fabricates a causal connection with no supporting evidence.